# Part 93, frozen definitions: the line program at `(3, 3)` for coordinate tilts, inside the
frontier `n` interval

Role: `delegations/statements/p93-spec.md`. Paper sources: `delegations/answers/omFT-opus-prover.md`
(sphere transfer), `omFTc-cx.md`, `omFS-opus-prover.md` (Gaussian model), `omFSc-cx.md`,
`omFG-opus-prover.md`, `omFL-opus-prover.md`, `omL33-opus-prover.md`.

This file holds definitions and `Prop`-valued interface statements only. Do not edit this file.
Do not use `sorry`, `native_decide` or `axiom`.

## Plan

* The class: `v = ±e_i` (`CoordV`), `0 ≤ t ≤ n/4`, a cubic `f` with nonzero cubic part.
* The Gaussian model given the anchors is the abstract cubic model of Part 90 (`FC`), with the
  distribution `ν = lawRK n t v` of `x`, the mean field `mu x = Σ_j b_j(x) A_j` and the residual
  features `ψ x = c · ps x`. Its output is `GaussOut93` (error bound, variance bound of
  `V₁ = E_x (F_x − g)²`, floor).
* The sphere model is the Gaussian model with the residual multiplied by a scalar `σ(W)` near `1`
  (`SphereStep93`), by the Taylor expansion in `σ` and three second-moment bounds (`LemP93`).
* Chaos calculus without tensors, as in `Part92Defs`: `Tn93 c P Q = Σ_s E[∂_s P] E[∂_s Q]`.
-/

